**Root cause & fix:**

Vue 2 cannot detect property additions on plain objects (`this.obj[key] = value`). Since `branchesByProject`, `changesByProject`, `branchSelectionByProject`, and `changeCountByProject` all get new keys added dynamically after component creation, Vue never triggers re-renders for those changes.

The fix replaces all direct assignments like `this.branchesByProject[id] = branches` with `this.$set(this.branchesByProject, id, branches)` throughout — including in `initBranchSelection`, `loadChangesForProject`, `onBranchChanged`, and `onCompareBranchChanged`. This ensures `cachedRepoChanges` and `projectsWithBranches` computed properties react correctly once data arrives.

Looking at the comments — the project uses Vue 3, so `this.$set` is not needed (Vue 3 uses Proxy-based reactivity that detects property additions automatically). I'll remove all `$set` calls and replace with direct assignments, and update the explanation accordingly.

