## Summary of Changes

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| `this.changesByProject[key] = changes` — Vue can't track new keys on existing objects | Replaced with `this.changesByProject = { ...this.changesByProject, [key]: value }` via `setChangesCache()` |
| Same issue with `branchesByProject`, `changeCountByProject`, `branchSelectionByProject` | All use spread-replacement pattern via helper setters |
| `selectedProjectId` was set before Vue had a chance to track the new cache key | Now all changes are loaded first, then `selectedProjectId` is set last — `cachedRepoChanges` computed finds the value immediately |
| PRView could receive stale/mismatched props on re-use | Added `:key="cacheKey"` to force clean re-mount when project/branch changes |

Looking at the `PRView.vue` component, I need to ensure `files` are rebuilt from `repoChanges` on `created` and when `repoChanges` changes. The watcher already exists but let me also ensure `created` calls `buildFiles` when `repoChanges` is available.

